add(['A1','V1'], 'Public DynamicVector and optimized FP32 storage mutations break shape invariants.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P1','correctness / memory safety','public default representations', ['Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/DynamicVector.swift:17','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/DynamicVector.swift:139','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector384Optimized.swift:156','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector512Optimized.swift:150','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector768Optimized.swift:150','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector1536Optimized.swift:150','Sources/VectorCore/Protocols/VectorProtocol.swift:38'], 'Fresh Ownership Release reports all four optimized views advertising 384/512/768/1536 values over four actual scalars. Original valid DynamicVector replacement probe is independently source-checked and replayed by root: dimension remains 2 with three storage elements; equality inspects dimension while hash traverses storage.', 'Do not say every vector or every check fails: generic Vector<D> uses a count-constrained DimensionStorage; FP16 conversions explicitly check malformed FP32 storage. No out-of-bounds write was executed. Different hash values are an observed consequence, not a mathematical guarantee against incidental hash collisions.', 'Enforce shape at owners: dynamic dimension derives from storage or a checked setter keeps it synchronized; fixed storage must preserve exact lane count through replacement and collection mutation. Reconsider protocol-wide settable storage.', 'Mechanical matrix for all families and wrappers: short/equal/long replacement and direct collection edits; dimension/count/buffer/serialization agree; equal values hash equally; invalid shapes are rejected before memory access. Test generic protocol mutation as well.',[])
add(['A1','RP additional: public invariant gap'], 'INT8 raw constructors, mutable storage, and synthesized Codable permit malformed fixed storage.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P1','correctness / memory safety','public opt-in INT8 APIs',['Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/QuantizedKernels.swift:140','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/QuantizedKernels.swift:164','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/QuantizedKernels.swift:177','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/QuantizedKernels.swift:190','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/QuantizedKernels.swift:461'], 'Ownership Release accepts one SIMD lane for a reported 512-dimensional vector. ShapeRoutes Release decodes storage:[] for 512/768/1536. Fixed-lane toFP32 reads follow directly from source. All four optimized FP32 decoders reject empty arrays as controls.', 'FP16 vectors are immutable and exact-length validated; they are not part of this shape defect. Invalid INT8 storage is observed; resulting unsafe reads are source-derived, not an executed memory fault. Synthesized decoding bypasses any future initializer-only fix.', 'Validate raw init and custom decoding; restrict storage mutation to shape-preserving operations, validate parameters separately.', 'Each INT8 width rejects short/long raw storage and JSON storage; valid round trips preserve dimension, payload and parameters. Exercise post-construction collection mutation and all unsafe conversion/kernel entry points.', ['OWN-01'])
add(['A2','IF5'], 'NormalizationHint retains metadata after direct wrapped mutation or a throwing mutable-buffer closure.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P1','correctness','public wrapper; inspected downstream consumers',['Sources/VectorCore/Integration/IndexableVector.swift:107','Sources/VectorCore/Integration/IndexableVector.swift:203','../VectorIndex/Sources/VectorIndex/TypedOverloads.swift:102','../VectorIndex/Sources/VectorIndex/TypedOverloads.swift:119','../future/VectorAccelerate/Sources/VectorAccelerate/Integration/KernelDistanceProviders.swift:189'], 'Fresh Release: initially valid [1,0] auto-hint changes to [2,0] through vector and reports normalized=true/magnitude1 while underlying magnitude2; buffer writes3 then throws and metadata remains1. Read downstream consumers using flags and cached inverse norms.', 'The initial hint is true, so this is not caller supplying a false assertion. GPU/downstream end-to-end behavior was not executed; existing contaminated indexes needing rebuild is conditional, not established deployment state.', 'Observe/restrict wrapped-value mutation and invalidate before mutable access or with defer. Explicitly define trust and value-semantics requirements for external conformers and decoded hints.', 'Test direct vector replacement/subscript/storage, wrapper storage, successful and throwing buffer mutation on every built-in representation; after changes metadata must be cleared or recomputed. Downstream insertion/query tests compare fresh normalized reference.', ['OWN-01'])
add(['A3','RP1'], 'SoAFP16Cache512 treats vector hash digests as exact candidate identity.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P1','correctness','public opt-in cache; no default or sibling caller found',['Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/SoAFP16Cache.swift:16','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/SoAFP16Cache.swift:94','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/SoAFP16Cache.swift:181','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector512Optimized.swift:334'], 'Fresh ShapeRoutes Release caches zero then independently changes each coordinate: 496 of512 changed inputs falsely hit; first/last eight miss. Root replays original returned-value corruption fixture.', 'Only the512 cache exists; 384/768/1536 key initializers are currently unused future surface. Full-coordinate hashing alone cannot turn a digest into an equality proof.', 'Use immutable candidate snapshot identity/version or compare complete contents on digest hits; retain order and candidate count in identity.', 'For every coordinate, reorder, count change and retained snapshot mutation, getOrCreate must match uncached conversion. Inject deliberate hash collisions to prove equality checking; repeated identical content still hits.', ['OWN-07'])
add(['C1','MS-1'], 'Compact-tier triangular matrix copies share later mutations.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P1','value semantics','public TriangularMatrix default sizes4...32; internal compact counts5...512',['Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:175','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:450','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TriangularMatrix.swift:94','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TriangularMatrix.swift:157'], 'Fresh actual-library Release verifies all508 compact element counts5...512 alias after copy/subscript write; public matrix n4,16,32 originals change99, controls3,33,64,65 stay1. CompactBuffer reference is shared while uniqueness inspects its nested ManagedBuffer.', 'Range is derived from m=n(n-1)/2; no claim for an arbitrary configured tier. Iterator snapshot and setAt exposure follow their same stored-copy/setter paths, not independent runtime reproduction.', 'Check uniqueness of the actual stored shared reference, not an inner property. Coordinate compact destruction repair.', 'COW tests across tier counts0,1,4,5,512,513,2048,2049 and matrix n3,4,32,33,64,65 for subscript,setAt,bulk and preexisting iterators; original unchanged and first mutation detaches once.', ['OWN-10','OWN-11'])
add(['C5','V3'], 'Binary in-place DynamicVector routes omit dimension checks.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P2','correctness / memory safety','public direct defaults and generic VectorProtocol operator dispatch',['Sources/VectorCore/Protocols/VectorProtocol.swift:181','Sources/VectorCore/Protocols/VectorProtocol.swift:194','Sources/VectorCore/Protocols/VectorProtocol.swift:230','Sources/VectorCore/Protocols/VectorProtocol.swift:241'], 'Fresh Release longer RHS yields add[5,7],subtract[-3,-3],Hadamard[4,10],generic +=[5,7],generic -=[-3,-3]. Source loops over lhs scalarCount with no check. Original Debug short-RHS fixture inspected; root owns replay.', 'Do not extend unchecked dispatch claim to concrete VectorFactory +=, which checks through +. Short RHS optimized overread is static reasoning; no Release overread was intentionally executed.', 'Shared dimension precondition before mutation on all three binary mutators; retain direct/generic consistency.', 'Equal/short/long RHS, empty combinations and direct/generic +=/-= plus all three methods. Invalid dimensions fail before any write; subprocess tests for trapping API or recoverable errors for checked API.', ['OWN-01'])
add(['PERF3','V5'], 'Optimized-vector hashes omit all but first and last eight scalar values.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P2','hash-table scaling','all four public optimized vector types; no vector-keyed downstream table found',['Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector384Optimized.swift:334','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector512Optimized.swift:334','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector768Optimized.swift:334','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector1536Optimized.swift:334'], 'Fresh Release across all four widths: interior-distinct values have identical hashes; signed-zero equality and hash both agree. Source combines exactly four SIMD4 values, giving deterministic same hash for all interior-only variation.', 'Legal Hashable collisions are a scaling issue, not equal-values-have-equal-hash violation. O(N^2*d) is worst-case equality work for sufficiently late differences, not measured universal cost. SIMD signed zero is not an additional bug.', 'Hash all equality-significant coordinates or choose explicit identity keys for consumers; repair cache exact identity separately.', 'Large structured/sparse interior-varying corpus must not deterministically collapse; equal values including signed zeros retain equal hashes. Coordinate Release insertion/lookup scaling measurement before speed claims.',[])
add(['C4','SIMD finding2'], 'Pointer normalization documents16-byte alignment as preferred but SIMD loads require it.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P2','unsafe API contract','public NormalizeKernels.normalizeUnchecked pointer overload',['Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/NormalizeKernels.swift:419','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/NormalizeKernels.swift:439'], 'Actual-library fresh Debug offset+4 from64-byte allocation traps at dimensions4,5,16,17: load from misaligned raw pointer. Dimension3 succeeds. Same actual Release fixtures all succeed on this ARM host.', 'Report Debug trap and source alignment precondition violation, not a reproduced Release failure. Dimension<4 does not enter SIMD loads. Caller meets documented Float capacity/nonzero magnitude obligations.', 'Use loadUnaligned or scalar/gather loads, or explicitly enforce and document mandatory SIMD alignment. A documentation-only compatibility tightening must be deliberate.', 'Offsets0,4,8,12 and dimensions0...5,15...17 in Debug/Release either compute correct finite unit values under supported inputs or reject consistently at a documented boundary; retain numerical reviewer coverage.',[])
add(['C17','V4'], 'Vector384Optimized permanently rebinds typed-owner memory where other widths restore binding.', 'qualified','P2','memory binding contract','normal public construction/toArray/buffer access',['Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector384Optimized.swift:69','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector384Optimized.swift:143','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector384Optimized.swift:156','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector384Optimized.swift:168'], 'Source comparison finds four permanent bindMemory sites versus scoped withMemoryRebound in512/768/1536. Swift UnsafeRawPointer migration guide and SE-0107 require later typed accesses to agree with current binding and describe restoring temporary bindings. No optimizer miscompile is reproduced.', 'Keep as binding-lifetime maintenance/contract finding. Layout compatibility is not a blanket strict-aliasing exemption; conversely merely seeing different spellings does not prove an observed miscompile. Alignment of Float-array source must be audited separately across all widths.', 'Use one reviewed conversion/borrow strategy across widths, restoring ownership binding; do not treat replacing the spelling alone as an alignment proof.', 'Mechanical audit of typed-owner rebinding, scoped nonescape and alignment obligations plus constructor/read/write/COW Release round trips for all widths. Document the permitted type/layout model.',[])
add(['MS-4'], 'Compact generic storage does not destroy manually initialized ManagedBuffer tail elements.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P2','memory lifetime','public TriangularMatrix<T>, default compact sizes4...32',['Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:380','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:406','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:418'], 'Fresh Release weak sentinel retained after matrices n4/32 leave scope; controls n3/33/65 release. CompactBuffer has no tail deinit; constructor and copy initialize count tail elements.', 'Reference-bearing arrays/strings follow missing generic destruction by source; only class sentinel was executed. A ManagedBuffer frees allocation but does not implicitly destroy manually initialized elements.', 'Destroy exactly initialized tail count at actual owner lifetime end; fix ownership sharing before choosing where deinit belongs.', 'Deinit/weak sentinel tests for all tiers, compact copy/detach/replacement/destruction and thrown access; each logical initialized reference released exactly once, no early destruction.', ['OWN-05'])
add(['C17','MS-5'], 'alignedCopy has incompatible initialize versus update semantics across alignment branches.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P2','unsafe API lifetime','public generic utility; no production caller found',['Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/MemoryUtilities.swift:135'], 'Original exact-source Token fixture inspected and replayed: old initialized destination leaks at offset0, releases at naturally aligned offset1. Code initialize(from:) vs destination[i]=source[i] admits no single destination-state contract for nontrivial T.', 'This is an unsafe API contract gap, not proof of a fault under a clearly documented supported destination state (none is supplied). Uninitialized-destination crash was not executed. Alignment here means preferred64-byte alignment, not natural-type misalignment.', 'Specify initialize or update semantics uniformly, preferably separate explicitly named APIs; separately document overlap.', 'Class/deinit and nontrivial-value tests at preferred and natural-only alignment, using only the chosen destination state. Identical lifetime behavior in both branches; overlap behavior explicitly tested if supported.',[])
add(['PERF1','MS-2'], 'HybridStorage repeating construction/fill performs quadratic buffer traffic.', 'confirmed-source','P2','allocation scaling','DynamicVector repeating/fill/resize above16 Float elements; explicit hybrid heap storage',['Sources/VectorCore/Storage/HybridStorage.swift:125','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/HybridStorage.swift:173','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/HybridStorage.swift:224','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/DynamicVector.swift:38','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/DynamicVector.swift:139'], 'Removed only integer counters from original COW fixture and verified full current source bodies occur byte-for-byte for UnifiedStorage,HybridStorage,DimensionStorage,VectorStorage. Replayed -O counter results: repeating512 514 normal+512 copy allocations=1026. Actual linked Release specialized ensureUnique and setter each retain before checking uniqueness, then allocate/copy; actual fill loops these paths. Excerpts retained.', 'Exact count1026 belongs to the instrumented fixture; actual Release instruction path independently proves duplicated ownership/copying and quadratic element traffic. Pointer addresses staying unchanged after writes do not refute copying: two replacement allocations can reuse prior address. SIMD stubs are not used to claim numerical results. Generic DimensionStorage default heap mutation does not inherit this finding.', 'Remove redundant outer COW ownership, mutate via exclusive ownership and fill once through a buffer. Preserve value semantics. Audit explicit DimensionStorage(.hybrid) as a dependency, separately from default heap.', 'Optimized allocation-scaling checks at Float16/17 and representative384/512/768/1536; unique scalar writes/fill stay bounded, shared first mutation detaches once, subsequent unique writes do not copy. No wall-clock speedup asserted until coordinated measurement.', ['OWN-05','OWN-14'])
add(['PERF1','MS-3'], 'TriangularMatrix scalar writes copy complete standard/aligned allocations even when uniquely owned.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P2','allocation scaling','public default matrix n>=33; original emphasized aligned n>=65',['Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:160','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:181','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:581','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TriangularMatrix.swift:225','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TriangularMatrix.swift:258'], 'Fresh actual Release:10 unique writes cause10 allocation-address changes at n33,64,65. Original exact-source aligned-copy counter replay gives10 copies at65. Standard setter extracts ContiguousArray and mutates while enum still owns it; aligned uniqueness method retains self. Full m-element copy per scalar gives O(m^2)=O(n^4) construction traffic.', 'Extend original exposure: standard tier513...2048 also detaches on scalar mutation, so repairing only AlignedBuffer.isUniquelyReferenced is insufficient. Address-change evidence uses integer addresses outside borrow scopes, not retained storage copies.', 'Fix compact/aligned ownership checks and standard enum extraction; add bulk construction after dormant bulk correctness is repaired.', 'Across all tier boundaries unique writes perform no full-buffer detaches; retained copy produces exactly one detach and remains unchanged. Construction traffic scales linearly with number of stored elements. Benchmark only after allocation and value-semantic checks.', ['OWN-05','OWN-14'])
add(['MS-6 standard/throwing bulk'], 'Dormant TieredStorage bulk access loses standard writes and inline writes on thrown closure exit.', 'confirmed-reproduced','P3','latent correctness','internal dormant mutable-buffer route; no production caller found',['Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:218','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:224','Sources/VectorCore/Utilities/TieredStorage.swift:365'], 'Fresh actual Release throwing closure writes19 then throws: counts1,4,513,2048 remain1; compact5/512 and aligned2049 retain19. Original ordinary-closure exact-source replay confirms standard513/2048 lose writes even without throw.', 'No current public matrix method routes through this bulk method. It becomes a required dependency if the proposed matrix bulk-fill optimization is introduced.', 'Persist modified standard payload with defer; make inline inner and outer copyback consistent on throws, or define a uniform rollback contract across every tier.', 'Normal and throwing closure tests at0,1,4,5,512,513,2048,2049 with retained original copies, consistent mutation policy and independent value semantics.', ['OWN-05'])
add(['MS-6 StorageSlice'], 'Internal StorageSlice returns scoped pointer without keeping its owner alive.', 'confirmed-source','P3','latent lifetime','internal dormant APIs; no production call found',['Sources/VectorCore/Storage/UnifiedStorage.swift:280','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/DimensionStorage.swift:298','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/UnifiedStorage.swift:259'], 'Slice only stores pointer/count returned from withUnsafeBufferPointer. Managed slice has no owner reference; inline DimensionStorage borrows a local tuple temporary. Current source call search finds declarations and forwarding only.', 'No supported-use UAF executed. This is distinct from DynamicVector.slice, which returns an owned vector.', 'Remove unused API or use scoped slice closures; an owning slice must hold storage and define snapshot/COW behavior, including inline storage promotion.', 'Compile-time nonescape design or scoped lifetime tests for inline/heap slices; no pointer survives its borrow. If retaining owner, prove owner retention and copy isolation.',[])
add(['MS-6 MoveOnlyStorage'], 'Experimental consuming into() returns memory still freed by deinit.', 'confirmed-source','P3','latent ownership transfer','internal compile gate MOVE_ONLY_EXPERIMENTAL absent from package settings',['Sources/VectorCore/Storage/UnifiedStorage.swift:10','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/UnifiedStorage.swift:36','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/UnifiedStorage.swift:66'], 'into returns the stored pointer, while unconditional deinit deallocates it; no transferred-state guard or deinit suppression is present.', 'Not compiled in ordinary builds and not runtime-reproduced. Do not enable this gate as an optimization without rederiving all lifetime paths.', 'Remove dormant experimental route or implement a real consuming transfer with exactly-once ownership handoff.', 'Gate-enabled separate fixture proves pointer survives consumed wrapper, is freed once by recipient, and nontransferred wrapper still frees correctly; audit every newly compiled branch.',[])
add(['RP additional: ownership contract gap'], 'Public FP16 pointer getters escape ContiguousArray borrow scopes.', 'qualified','P2','unsafe API lifetime','public opt-in fp16Storage getters; kernels use scoped borrows',['Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/MixedPrecisionKernels.swift:344','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/MixedPrecisionKernels.swift:387','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/MixedPrecisionKernels.swift:430'], 'All three getters return baseAddress from withUnsafeBufferPointer. Returned UnsafePointer has no lifetime token; temporary owner expressions can end storage lifetime. Source traced; no UAF executed.', 'The getter is explicitly unsafe; do not equate pointer return with a demonstrated supported-use corruption. Retaining the array owner alone does not change the documented nonescape condition of withUnsafeBufferPointer.', 'Provide scoped FP16 storage access; deprecate or precisely document any persistent pointer API with owned allocation design.', 'All direct kernels and callers use scoped borrows or explicit owned allocation lifetime. Temporary-expression use cannot silently escape through new safe API. Test512/768/1536 content and owner lifetime.',[])
add(['RP additional: cache capacity'], 'SoAFP16Cache512 accepts nonpositive maxSize then evicts from an empty list.', 'confirmed-source','P3','boundary validation','public explicit cache configuration; default100 unaffected',['Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/SoAFP16Cache.swift:85','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/SoAFP16Cache.swift:133'], 'With size0 and empty cache, cache.count>=maxSize is true and accessOrder.removeFirst traps. Same proof holds negative capacity; original zero subprocess reproduced by root/reduced-precision reviewer.', 'Lower priority configuration boundary. Choose whether zero intentionally disables caching before testing desired policy.', 'Precondition positive capacity or implement zero retention policy; reject negative.', 'Fresh empty/nonempty stores at negative,zero,one capacities have documented behavior, repeated eviction and statistics remain consistent.',[])
add(['PERF8 FP16 cache','RP additional: retention'], 'FP16 cache caps entry count while payload bytes scale with candidates per entry.', 'confirmed-source','P2 opportunity','memory scaling','public opt-in512 cache',['Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/SoAFP16Cache.swift:49','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/SoAFP16Cache.swift:75','Sources/VectorCore/Operations/Kernels/MixedPrecisionKernels.swift:468'], '512*2*N=1024N logical payload bytes per entry;100 million-candidate entries yield102400000000 bytes before padding/keys. Comment1KB per100 vectors understates logical100KiB by100x. Key map is O(N); accessOrder firstIndex/remove O(entry count).', 'Sizing derivation, not attempted allocation/RSS measurement; immutable COW cache values are not themselves an actor data race.', 'Byte admission/eviction budget and byte statistics; correct size docs and account for metadata/padding.', 'Tests with small byte budget cap retained payload; oversized entries follow explicit policy; statistics and eviction accounting agree with logical/allocated sizes. No claim of measured RSS.', ['OWN-04'])
