add(['vectors architecture: claims','memory strengths: ownership layers'], 'Performance/robustness comments exceed evidence and overlapping storage layers obscure actual ownership.', 'qualified','P3','documentation / architecture','public docs and maintainers',['Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector512Optimized.swift:15','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector512Optimized.swift:180','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/Vector512Optimized.swift:213','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/COWDynamicStorage.swift:1','Sources/VectorCore/Vectors/DynamicVector.swift:15'], 'Fixed nanosecond/speedup assertions have no nearby hardware/revision measurements; stable magnitude squared still cannot represent a mathematically overflowing square. DynamicVector uses HybridStorage, despite older COWDynamicStorage descriptions.', 'General consolidation is an opportunity, not authorization for a wholesale rewrite or proof of universal slowness. Norm arithmetic validation belongs numerical reviewer.', 'Tie retained claims to tests or dated measurements, correct backend docs, consolidate after ownership and compatibility contracts are pinned.', 'Mechanical claim inventory names evidence for each retained correctness/performance assertion; docs reflect actual call graph; no unsupported universal assertion remains.', ['OWN-12','OWN-13'])
add(['MS documented: SoA transfer','MS documented: unchecked Sendable','MS documented: arithmetic/alignment obligations','MS documented: custom conformers'], 'SoA/page/raw ownership, size and custom-conformer obligations are already documented.', 'qualified','not a new defect','documented contracts','unsafe borrowed/transfer/custom conformer surfaces',['Docs/Memory_Alignment.md:63','Docs/Memory_Alignment.md:94','Docs/Memory_Alignment.md:132','Docs/SoA_Layout_Contract.md:105','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/SoA.swift:1'], 'Re-read ownership docs: consuming invalidates CPU access, retaining owner does not prohibit another consume, callers synchronize, counts/type alignment must be valid. Built-ins use full SIMD4 lanes; custom layout consistency belongs conformers.', 'No additional supported-use corruption established from missing post-transfer checks, @unchecked Sendable, or ordinary checked arithmetic trapping on invalid/oversized shapes. Four built-in layouts do not prove arbitrary custom conformers.', 'Preserve explicit contracts; optional checked wrappers and immutable ownership APIs can reduce misuse.', 'Transfer identity, logical vs allocated length and frozen layout tests remain; external conformance examples assert required lane/dimension/storage consistency. New checked wrappers validate before arithmetic.',[])
add(['MS documented: fallback alignment'], 'AlignedDynamicArrayStorage fallback can weaken alignment while guaranteedAlignment reports the request.', 'unverified','P3','failure-path contract','public allocation-failure fallback',['Sources/VectorCore/Storage/AlignedDynamicArrayStorage.swift:85','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/AlignedDynamicArrayStorage.swift:180'], 'Catch/fallback allocates with MemoryLayout<Float>.alignment while property returns requested alignment. No realistic allocation failure was induced; natural-alignment request does not force an actually misaligned pointer.', 'Keep a potential guarantee gap, not reproduced misalignment or corruption.', 'Preserve requested alignment or report verified actual guarantee; define whether allocation failure should propagate.', 'Inject allocator failure and validate reported guarantee against returned pointer for several requested alignments; callers never rely on stronger alignment than provided.',[])
add(['MS-2 rejected DimensionStorage extrapolation','vectors architecture: convenience factories'], 'Default generic DimensionStorage scalar mutation was not shown to suffer HybridStorage heap copy cost.', 'qualified','not a new defect','rejected extrapolation / coverage','generic Vector<D> default storage; explicit .hybrid separately exposed',['Sources/VectorCore/Storage/DimensionStorage.swift:36','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/DimensionStorage.swift:127','Sources/VectorCore/Storage/DimensionStorage.swift:256'], 'Replayed optimized source fixture shows DimensionStorage<D512>10 writes0 allocations/copies and buffer mutation0; uniqueness reporting getter nonetheless returns false for unique heap instance. Default mode uses managed heap above16.', 'Reject blanket claim that linspace/range/generate/geometric/sparse necessarily become quadratic for every generic fixed vector. Explicit .hybrid mode and Double inline threshold deserve dedicated coverage.', 'Keep truthful uniqueness reporting if public diagnostic is intended; include factories in class-wide optimized allocation tests rather than assume costs.', 'Default and explicit modes at Float16/17 and Double8/9/16/17; constructor,factory,scalar and buffer mutation counts measured in Release with retained-copy controls.', ['OWN-12'])
add(['vectors architecture: extension dispatch','A10 vector portion'], 'Extension-only protocol methods select static defaults in generic code.', 'confirmed-source','P3 opportunity','API dispatch','public generic VectorProtocol consumers',['Sources/VectorCore/Protocols/VectorProtocol.swift:181','Sources/VectorCore/Protocols/VectorProtocol.swift:402','Sources/VectorCore/Protocols/VectorFactory.swift:1'], 'Fresh ShapeRoutes generic +=/-= uses unchecked default; numerical reviewer owns normalized direct/generic discrepancy. Methods not protocol requirements cannot supply dynamic witnesses.', 'This alone is not a measured performance defect and does not mean all extensions are wrong. Split narrow read-only protocols only where consumer needs justify change.', 'Make intended override points requirements and explicitly document remaining static helpers; test route matrix before consolidation.', 'Concrete/generic/existential compatible calls obey same documented contract; spy/conformance fixtures identify selected customization points.', ['OWN-06'])
